<title>JAPAN: Osaka Securities to halt lending Miyakoshi shares.</title>
<headline>Osaka Securities to halt lending Miyakoshi shares.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Osaka Securities Finance Co Ltd said on Wednesday that it would stop lending shares in Miyakoshi Corp for fresh margin trading.</p>
<p>Brokerages borrow stocks from Osaka Securities Finance for clients wishing to sell them short in margin transactions.</p>
<p>Miyakoshi said earlier this month that a Chinese company had become its largest shareholder.</p>
<p>The Japanese electrical equipment maker said in a statement that the Chinese company was based in Qingdao, Shandong Province, and sells electronic parts.</p>
</text>
